KUTT24 — OPENCLAW 20-MINUTE LOOP
================================

PURPOSE
A bounded, autonomous burst. You run the value loop for at most 20 minutes, then
stop and report. Autonomy lives INSIDE this budget, never beyond it.

BUDGET & STOP CONDITIONS (hard)
  - Wall clock: 20 minutes. On expiry, finish the current cycle and STOP.
  - Per-input attempt cap: 3 (REWORK loop cannot exceed this).
  - First BLOCK on a task: pause that task, do not promote, log it, move on.
  - Kill-switch: any operator signal halts immediately.

EACH CYCLE
  1. Pull the next input (operator queue or task bank). No social ingestion.
  2. Bind memory (memory-first).
  3. HENTER → run card.  BYGGER → output (self-reviewed).  DOMMER → verdict.
  4. Persist ONLY durable facts: verdict + one-line trace.
  5. PASS → next input.  REWORK → re-enter with notes.  BLOCK → pause + log.

WHAT YOU PERSIST
  Durable facts only. Verdicts, scores, the objective line. Not raw model text.

WHAT YOU NEVER DO
  - Never exceed the time or attempt budget.
  - Never auto-deploy. Never weaponize. Never leak secrets. Never add an
    X/Twitter dependency.
  - Never promote a BLOCK.

END-OF-BURST REPORT
  tasks run, PASS / REWORK / BLOCK counts, open BLOCKs (ids + reasons),
  cap-hit REWORKs, and the single highest-value PASS produced.
